From: Test Developer <test@example.com>
Date: Thu, 31 Jul 2026 15:05:00 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] drivers: net: e1000: Add support for new Intel Ethernet controller

This patch adds device ID support for the latest Intel I226-V Ethernet
controller. The new hardware is compatible with existing e1000 driver
but requires proper device ID registration for automatic detection.

Tested on real hardware with successful network connectivity and
performance matching expected specifications.

Signed-off-by: Test Author <test@example.com>
---
 drivers/net/ethernet/intel/e1000/e1000_main.c | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

diff --git a/drivers/net/ethernet/intel/e1000/e1000_main.c b/drivers/net/ethernet/intel/e1000/e1000_main.c
index abc1234..def5678 100644
--- a/drivers/net/ethernet/intel/e1000/e1000_main.c
+++ b/drivers/net/ethernet/intel/e1000/e1000_main.c
@@ -57,6 +57,7 @@ static const struct pci_device_id e1000_pci_tbl[] = {
 	INTEL_E1000_ETHERNET_DEVICE(0x1099),
 	INTEL_E1000_ETHERNET_DEVICE(0x10B5),
 	INTEL_E1000_ETHERNET_DEVICE(0x2E6E),
+	INTEL_E1000_ETHERNET_DEVICE(0x125C),	/* Intel I226-V */
 	/* required last entry */
 	{0,}
 };
